\section{Chirality on Tetrahedra}

For a tetrahedron \(T_i = (V_{i0}, V_{i1}, V_{i2}, V_{i3})\), define edge vectors
\[
\mathbf{e}_1 = V_{i1} - V_{i0}, \quad
\mathbf{e}_2 = V_{i2} - V_{i0}, \quad
\mathbf{e}_3 = V_{i3} - V_{i0}.
\]

The chirality \(\chi_i\) is defined as the scalar triple product
\[
\chi_i = \det[\mathbf{e}_1, \mathbf{e}_2, \mathbf{e}_3]
      = \mathbf{e}_1 \cdot (\mathbf{e}_2 \times \mathbf{e}_3).
\]

Parity-violating modes correspond to sign changes
\[
\chi_i \mapsto -\chi_i
\]
under orientation reversal.